  "tagline": "A highland town of 11 churches carved straight down into solid rock",
  "intro": "Lalibela sits about 2,500 m up in Ethiopia's northern highlands. Its 11 medieval churches were not built but hewn out of the volcanic rock, mostly in the 12th and 13th centuries, and tradition credits King Gebre Meskel Lalibela of the Zagwe dynasty. They are still working churches and one of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Ethiopian Orthodox Christianity.",
