  "facts": [
   "Tradition says King Lalibela set out to build a second Jerusalem in Ethiopia, and the churches' layout and names symbolically echo Jerusalem.",
   "Biete Medhane Alem is believed to be the largest monolithic church in the world.",
   "The Church of Saint George (Bete Giyorgis) is cut in the shape of a cross and is considered the most finely executed and best preserved of the group.",
   "The dating is still debated: one archaeologist argues some of the churches were carved around 600 to 800 CE, centuries before King Lalibela.",
   "Many churches have wells beside them, fed by an artesian system that brings water up to the ridge the town sits on."
  ],
  "bestTime": "October to March (dry season). Genna (Jan 7) and Timkat (Jan 19) bring huge pilgrim crowds.",
  "gettingThere": "Fly Ethiopian Airlines from Newark to Addis Ababa (about 13 to 14 hours), then take a roughly one-hour domestic flight to Lalibela.",
  "tip": "Check the State Department advisory first: the Amhara region has seen fighting since 2023. Go with a local guide, and bring socks since shoes come off inside every church."
